# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository.
#
# Without this, a file authored on Windows can land in a commit with CRLF while every other file
# has LF. That builds fine locally -- spotless resolves line endings platform-natively -- and then
# fails only in CI on Linux, which is an expensive way to find out. BudgetService.java did exactly
# that.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
